\title{Naming policy for the searchnet API}
\description{
New exported functions use the \code{searchnet_} prefix. Names that begin with
\code{saomnk_} are frozen: no new \code{saomnk_} functions are added, and existing
ones keep their names, arguments, and return values. Where several
\code{saomnk_} functions drew variants of one plot, a single \code{searchnet_}
function now selects the variant with an argument
(\code{\link[=searchnet_plot_exploration]{searchnet_plot_exploration()}}, \code{\link[=searchnet_plot_multiwave]{searchnet_plot_multiwave()}}), and names
that carried a version or development tag have a descriptive replacement
(\code{\link[=searchnet_plot_cumulative_entry]{searchnet_plot_cumulative_entry()}}, \code{\link[=searchnet_plot_new_component_shocks]{searchnet_plot_new_component_shocks()}}).
}
\details{
The superseded names remain exported as thin wrappers that forward to the
replacement and return the same object. Each emits a deprecation warning
the first time it is called in a session, not on every call, so a script
that loops over one is not buried in repeats. The wrappers stay at least
until one minor release after the SAOM-NK software paper in the Journal of
Statistical Software is accepted. The full old-to-new mapping is in
\link{searchnet-deprecated-plots}.
}
\section{API classes}{

Every exported function belongs to one of five classes: \emph{core}
(simulation, the estimation bridge, the \{K\} framework, diagnostics and
causal tools), \emph{visualization} (plots, themes, palettes, and exporters for
animation), \emph{teaching} (classroom and strategy-game workflows), \emph{legacy}
(the deprecated wrappers described above), and \emph{advanced} (exported but
documented as internal; candidates to stop exporting in a future minor
release). The full list, with each function's class and help topic, is
generated from \code{NAMESPACE} and the help pages and ships as
\code{system.file("API_CLASSIFICATION.md", package = "searchnet")}.
